# Mimir IS a secret scanner. Its test fixtures and research notes intentionally
# contain realistic secret patterns (AWS keys, GitHub/Slack/Stripe tokens, PEM
# keys, connection strings) so the scanner's own rules can be tested against
# authentic inputs. Exclude these paths from semgrep so security tooling does
# not flag the project's REQUIRED test data — and so contributors are not
# tempted to weaken fixtures to evade a scanner that should never have scanned
# them in the first place.
testdata/
.planning/

# Test files frequently embed fixture secret literals inline for table tests.
*_test.go
